   "text": {
    "L1": "The Collatz game repeats one simple rule. Every starting number gets checked by its parity.",
    "L2": "For an even number, divide by 2. For an odd number, multiply by 3 and add 1.",
    "L3": "Starting at 9 gives 28, 14, and 7. Continuing the rule eventually reaches 1.",
    "L4": "After 1, the sequence loops 4, 2, 1, 4, 2, 1. The rule can keep repeating.",
    "L5": "A bigger starting number does not always take more steps. Seven takes 16 steps, but 32 takes only 5.",
    "L6": "People have tried many starting numbers, and every one tried reaches 1. But this is not a proof.",
    "L7": "The Collatz conjecture says every number reaches 1. It is still an unsolved problem.",
    "L8": "Now choose which starting number takes more steps to reach 1."
   },
